====================================================================================================================
K  THE KICK PHYSICS: the unbinding relation, I27, and an idealised static single-halo model
====================================================================================================================
    exact, isotropic kick: f_unbound = clip(((v_o + v_k)^2 - v_esc^2) / (4 v_o v_k), 0, 1).  f = 1 (every direction) iff v_k >= v_o + v_esc (I27's hypothesis); f = 1/2 iff v_k^2 = v_esc^2 - v_o^2 (the kick supplies the binding energy); f = 0 iff v_k <= v_esc - v_o
    at rest (v_o = 0)                           : every daughter unbound for v_esc <= 1.000 v_k (575-650 km/s); half at v_esc = 1.000 v_k; none for v_esc >= 1.000 v_k
    circular, point mass (v_o = v_esc/sqrt2)    : every daughter unbound for v_esc <= 0.586 v_k (337-381 km/s); half at v_esc = 1.414 v_k; none for v_esc >= 3.414 v_k
    marginally bound infall (v_o = v_esc)       : every daughter unbound for v_esc <= 0.500 v_k (288-325 km/s); half at v_esc = never below half (f >= 1/2 + v_k/(4 v_esc)); none for v_esc >= never
    => v_esc = v_k/2 is the every-direction (I27) edge ONLY for daughters moving at the escape speed; the half-unbinding point is set by the binding energy, v_k = sqrt(v_esc^2 - v_o^2), which for bound orbits means v_esc >= v_k
    static model, v_k 575: 50% retained at v200 = 264 km/s (Phi(inf)) / 356 km/s (Phi(2 r200)) = 0.46 / 0.62 v_k;  canonical floor at v200 218 / 270
    static model, v_k 600: 50% retained at v200 = 275 km/s (Phi(inf)) / 372 km/s (Phi(2 r200)) = 0.46 / 0.62 v_k;  canonical floor at v200 227 / 283
    static model, v_k 625: 50% retained at v200 = 287 km/s (Phi(inf)) / 388 km/s (Phi(2 r200)) = 0.46 / 0.62 v_k;  canonical floor at v200 237 / 295
    static model, v_k 650: 50% retained at v200 = 298 km/s (Phi(inf)) / 404 km/s (Phi(2 r200)) = 0.46 / 0.62 v_k;  canonical floor at v200 247 / 307
    => the idealised static halo puts half-retention at v200 = 264-404 km/s (overlapping the cap band 247-361); the construction's committed retention (L388, with assembly) puts it at v200 = 737-866 km/s, x1.8-3.3 the static values

