VERDICT
====================================================================================================================
  THE TRANSITION.  The committed retention (L388, pooled, >= 6e13 Msun/h) crosses 50% at v_c(1 Mpc/h) = 702-849 km/s
  over v_k = 575-650 (v200 737-866; Phi(inf) escape speed at 1 Mpc/h 1306-1619): x2.2-2.6 v_cap,
  x1.22-1.31 v_k, and an escape speed x4.5-5.0 v_k/2.  The canonical X-COP floor is crossed at v_c
  588-714 (flags ['extrap', 'in', 'in', 'in']).  The lowest plausible 50% crossing (any estimator, bootstrap 2.5%,
  any box, any circular convention incl. both footings' v_f) is 602 km/s, against the cap band's top 361 km/s.
  THE EMPTIED END.  The kick empties hosts up to v200 ~ 264 km/s whose pre-decay escape speeds reach 494 (r200) and
  886 km/s (centre), i.e. deeper than v_k/2; the edge itself lies in the unmeasured gap 264-531 km/s.
  THE KICK.  v_cap / v_k = 0.50-0.57: "about half the kick" holds as arithmetic.  v_esc = v_k/2 is I27's every-direction
  edge only for daughters moving at the escape speed; half-unbinding needs v_k^2 = v_esc^2 - v_o^2.  The idealised static halo puts
  half-retention at v200 264-404 (near v_k/2); the construction's runs (with assembly) at v200 737-866.
  MS3's OWN ROWS.  A retention step AT the cap scale (v200 = 337 km/s): 1.64/1.74 at the 1.75 Mpc cap
  (FAILS the 1.2 gate); its largest passing cap is ~206 km/s = x0.61 the step.
  VERDICT: the two scales DO NOT COINCIDE.

